# Build context is the repo root (see apps/website/docker/Dockerfile).
.git
.github
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.svelte-kit
**/.vite
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report

# Website submodules have their own build contexts
apps/website/cryptify
apps/website/postguard

# Local env overrides never belong in an image
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/*.pem

**/.DS_Store
# Scoped to the add-in, NOT `**/.env`: apps/website commits its .env (it carries
# the VITE_FILEHOST_URL placeholder its entrypoint substitutes at container
# start), and excluding it globally fails the website image build with
# "Missing required environment variable: VITE_FILEHOST_URL". This replaces the
# app-local .dockerignore that went dead when the build context moved to the root.
apps/outlook-addon/.env
apps/outlook-addon/.env.*

# Also carried over from that app-local file: docs and READMEs are in the build
# context otherwise, so `COPY apps/outlook-addon/ apps/outlook-addon/` busts the
# source layer and forces a full webpack pass on a docs-only edit. Nothing under
# these is read by the build, and the runtime stage only copies dist/.
apps/outlook-addon/docs
apps/outlook-addon/CLAUDE.md
apps/outlook-addon/README.md
apps/outlook-addon/*.log
